OFFICE OF THE KAZEKAGE -- SUNAGAKURE POSITION FOR THE FIVE KAGE SUMMIT
Prepared for Lord Gaara, Fifth Kazekage. Confidential.

The Five Kage Summit convenes the leaders of the Sand, Leaf, Mist, Cloud, and
Stone to address the shared threat posed by the Akatsuki and the hunting of the
tailed beasts.

Sunagakure's declared positions:
1. Full support for a unified allied response. As the village that suffered the
   abduction of its own Kazekage-jinchuriki, Sunagakure speaks from experience
   of the Akatsuki threat and will not stand apart.
2. Protection of all jinchuriki as a collective duty of the five villages, not
   the burden of each village alone.
3. Reaffirmation of the Sand-Leaf alliance as a model for broader cooperation.

Lord Gaara attends in person, accompanied by his guard detail. His counsel: the
old age of villages warring in isolation invited this crisis; only a shinobi
alliance can answer it. The Kazekage is authorized to commit Sand forces to a
joint command. Filed to the Kazekage Office.
